    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61686" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαῖτμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, poet. Noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>depth</i> or <i>gulf</i> of the sea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα λ. θαλάσσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.504
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				5.174
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.260
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλὸς ἐς μέγα λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					19.267
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.561
			</span></i>; also alone, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. μέγ᾽ ἐκπερόωσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.35
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.409
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.276
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				13.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1299
			</span></i>.</div>
